  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\nFrom French \"début.\"\n\nUSAGE:\nデビュー is commonly used in the entertainment industry for an artist's first release or performance. In casual usage, it is applied humorously or affectionately to any first experience: {社会人|しゃかいじん}デビュー (entering the workforce for the first time), {保育園|ほいくえん}デビュー (a child's first day at nursery), {公園|こうえん}デビュー (a new parent's first visit to the local park).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- デビューする: to make one's debut\n- メジャーデビュー: major (label) debut\n- デビュー{作|さく}: debut work\n- デビュー{曲|きょく}: debut single/song\n- {社会人|しゃかいじん}デビュー: entering the workforce",
